    "title": "Berkeley police nab suspect stealing from high-end activewear store - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Aaron Tolentino ,\n56 minutes ago\n( KRON ) — The Berkeley Police Department announced Wednesday it made an arrest after a theft over the weekend. According to BPD, an automated license plate reader (APLR) helped an officer track down a retail theft suspect.\nA social media post by BPD regarding the arrest included a photo of where the alleged theft happened. The photo shows that the incident occurred at the Lululemon store on Fourth Street. BPD did not specify what was stolen or how much the value of the stolen goods was.\nKatie Porter goes viral for cutting CBS interview short after question on Trump voters BPD arrested the suspect on Tuesday after the department was alerted via APLR that the suspect vehicle in the initial theft over the weekend had reentered the city. Police said the suspect was “in the process of stealing from another local retailer.”\nThe suspect, who BPD did not identify, was taken into custody for both incidents.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KRON4.\n2",
